window.DH=window.DH||{};window.DH["e01"]={"id":"e01","title":"第一集","parts":[{"id":"p01","title":"Mary Alice 出场","lines":[{"id":"e01p0101","s":"Alice","t":"My name is Mary Alice Young.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0102","s":"Alice","t":"When you read this morning's paper, you may come across an article about the unusual day I had last week.","r":true,"m":["come across 偶然遇见 come across an article"]},{"id":"e01p0103","s":"Alice","t":"Normally, there's never anything newsworthy about my life, but that all changed last Thursday.","r":true,"m":["newsworthy 有新闻价值的 there's never anything newsworthy about my life."]},{"id":"e01p0104","s":"Alice","t":"Of course, everything seemed quite normal at first.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0105","s":"Alice","t":"I made breakfast for my family,","r":true},{"id":"e01p0106","s":"Alice","t":"I performed my chores.","r":true,"m":["chore n.家庭杂务，杂活；累活，苦差事 日常多用复数 chores","I performed my chores. 我做了我的家务"]},{"id":"e01p0107","s":"Alice","t":"I completed my projects.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0108","s":"Alice","t":"I ran my errands.","r":true,"m":["ran errands 跑腿，办事  I ran my errands. “我办了点事。” 或者 “我处理了一些琐事。”"]},{"id":"e01p0109","s":"Alice","t":"In truth, I spent the day as I spent every other day, quietly polishing the routine of my life until it gleamed with perfection.","r":true,"m":["In truth 真实地，说实话，事实上","polish 擦亮；改进","routine 常规，惯例","gleam 发微光，闪烁；显得光洁明亮 until it gleamed with perfection. 直至完美"]},{"id":"e01p0110","s":"Alice","t":"That's why it was so astonishing when I decided to go to my hallway closet and retrieve a revolver that had never been used.","r":true,"m":["astonish 使吃惊，使惊讶 That's why it was so astonishing...","hallway closet走廊壁橱 hallway 门厅，走廊；过道 closet 壁橱，储藏室","retrieve 找回，收回,本句语境是从壁橱里取出、拿出","revolver 左轮手枪；旋转器"]},{"id":"e01p0111","s":"Alice","t":"My body was discovered by my neighbor, Mrs. Martha Huber, who'd been startled by a strange popping sound.","r":true,"m":["startle 使吓一跳，使惊奇"]},{"id":"e01p0112","s":"Alice","t":"Her curiosity aroused, Mrs. Huber tried to think of a reason for dropping in on me unannounced.","r":true,"m":["curiosity 好奇心，求知欲","arouse 引起，激起；叫醒 Her curiosity aroused.","think of a reason 想出一个理由","drop in on sb unannounced. 不请自来 drop in on sb 突然拜访某人 unannounced  突然的；未经宣布的；未通知的"]},{"id":"e01p0113","s":"Alice","t":"After some initial hesitation, she decided to return the blender she had borrowed from me six months before.","r":true,"m":["initial adj. 开始的，最初的；","hesitation 犹豫，不情愿","blender 搅拌机","ago = 以现在为基准 ↔ 只用一般过去时 before = 以过去某一刻为基准 ↔ 常用过去完成时"]},{"id":"e01p0114","s":"Huber","t":"It's my neighbor. I think she's been shot. There's blood everywhere. ","r":true},{"id":"e01p0115","s":"Huber","t":"Yes, you've got to send an ambulance. You've got to send one right now.","r":true,"m":["have got to 不得不，必须","ambulance 救护车"]},{"id":"e01p0116","s":"Alice","t":"And for a moment, Mrs. Huber stood motionless in her kitchen, grief-stricken by this senseless tragedy. ","r":true,"m":["motionless 静止的；不运动的 stood motionless 站立不动","grief-stricken 极度悲伤的 grief 悲伤，悲痛 stricken 受灾的，患病的","senseless 愚蠢的；无知觉的；无意识的","tragedy n. 悲惨事件，惨剧；悲剧（作品）；不幸，遗憾；"]},{"id":"e01p0117","s":"Alice","t":"But, only for a moment.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0118","s":"Huber","t":"If there was one thing Mrs. Huber was known for, it was her ability to look on the bright side.","r":true,"m":["bright 明亮的；鲜艳的；聪明的；欢快的，有活力的；光明的，有希望的；","look on the bright side 往好处想、乐观看待事物"]}]},{"id":"p02","title":"Lynette 出场","lines":[{"id":"e01p0201","s":"Alice","t":"I was laid to rest on a Monday.","r":true,"m":["lay 安放，放置；铺放，铺设；下（蛋），产（卵） -> laid -> laid","lay to rest 安葬，埋葬; 结束，解决; 使平静，使安心"]},{"id":"e01p0202","s":"Alice","t":"After the funeral, all the residents of Wisteria Lane came to pay their respects.","r":true,"m":["funeral 葬礼，丧礼","resident n.居民 adj. 居住的，居留的 residence n. 住宅，住所","Wisteria Lane 紫藤巷   wisteria 紫藤   lane 小路","pay one's respects 表示敬意"]},{"id":"e01p0203","s":"Alice","t":"And, as people do in these situations, they brought food.","r":true,"m":["as 连词，后面可以接完整从句（主语 + 谓语）like 介词，后面只能接名词/代词"]},{"id":"e01p0204","s":"Alice","t":"Lynette Scavo brought fried chicken.","r":true,"m":["fried chicken 炸鸡"]},{"id":"e01p0205","s":"Alice","t":"Lynette had a great family recipe for fried chicken.","r":true,"m":["recipe 烹饪法，食谱；诀窍，秘诀；原因；"]},{"id":"e01p0206","s":"Alice","t":"Of course, she didn't cook much while she was moving up the corporate ladder. She didn't have the time.","r":true,"m":["move up the corporate ladder 向上爬梯子：指在公司或组织中逐步晋升到更高的职位或地位。","corporate 公司的；法人的；共同的，全体的","ladder 梯子；（职位晋升的）阶梯","while 多接延续性动作 when 既可接短暂动作，也可接延续动作"]},{"id":"e01p0207","s":"Alice","t":"But when her doctor announced Lynette was pregnant, her husband Tom had an idea.","r":true,"m":["pregnant adj. 怀孕的，妊娠的"]},{"id":"e01p0208","s":"Alice","t":"Why not quit your job? Kids do better with stay-at-home moms, so it would be so much less stressful.","r":true,"m":["Why not...? 口语省略句=Why don't you...?"]},{"id":"e01p0209","s":"Alice","t":"But this was not the case.","r":true,"m":["not the case. 不是这样的"]},{"id":"e01p0210","s":"Alice","t":"In fact, Lynette's life had become so hectic, she was now forced to get her fried chicken from the fast-food restaurant.","r":true,"m":["hectic 繁忙的，忙乱的；","be forced to 被迫"]},{"id":"e01p0211","s":"Alice","t":"Lynette would've appreciated the irony if she'd stopped to think about it.","r":true,"m":["appreciate 欣赏，鉴赏；理解，明白；感谢，感激；升值，增值","irony （出乎意料的）奇异可笑之处，具有讽刺意味的情况；反语，讽刺","Lynette would've appreciated the irony if she'd stopped to think about it. 如果勒奈特当时停下来思考一下，她就会体会到其中的讽刺意味了","would have done + if 从句 had done 结构，描述与过去事实相反的假设"]},{"id":"e01p0212","s":"Alice","t":"But she couldn't. She didn't have the time.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0213","s":"Lynette","t":"No, you are going to behave today. I am not going to be humiliated in front of the entire neighborhood. And, just so you know how serious I am...","r":true,"m":["behave 行为，表现；起反应，起作用；守规矩，举止得体","humiliate 羞辱，使蒙羞","entire 全部的，整个的；完全的，绝对的","serious 严重的，危急的；认真的，严肃的；重要的，须重视的","just so you know 只是让你知道"]},{"id":"e01p0214","s":"Boy","t":"What's that?","r":true},{"id":"e01p0215","s":"Lynette","t":"Santa's cell-phone number.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0216","s":"Boy","t":"How did you get that?","r":true},{"id":"e01p0217","s":"Lynette","t":"I know someone who knows someone who knows an elf.","r":true,"m":["elf （神话故事中的）小精灵，小妖精"]},{"id":"e01p0218","s":"Lynette","t":"And if any of you acts up, so help me, I will call Santa. I will tell him you want socks for Christmas.","r":true,"m":["act up 行为不端，调皮捣蛋；功能失常，出毛病；恶化，加重","so help me 发誓，诚心诚意"]},{"id":"e01p0219","s":"Lynette","t":"Are you willing to risk that?","r":true},{"id":"e01p0220","s":"Lynette","t":"OK, let's get this over with.","r":true,"m":["Let's get this over with 让我们赶快结束这一切吧","get it over with 尽快完成某事，特别是为了让不愉快的事情尽快过去"]}]},{"id":"p03","title":"Gabrielle 出场","lines":[{"id":"e01p0301","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle Solis, who lives down the block, brought a spicy paella.","r":true,"m":["block 大块，一块；街区；大楼 down the block 沿着这条街往那头、街那头","paella （西班牙的）肉菜饭 spicy paella"]},{"id":"e01p0302","s":"Alice","t":"Since her modeling days in New York, Gabrielle had developed a taste for rich food and rich men.","r":true,"m":["develop a taste for 培养对……的喜好：逐渐形成对某种事物的兴趣或喜爱。"]},{"id":"e01p0303","s":"Alice","t":"Carlos, who worked in mergers and acquisitions, proposed on their third date.","r":true,"m":["work in mergers and acquisitions 从事兼并与收购业务 merger （公司、组织的）合并acquisition 学得；获取；购买，添置；收购，购置的产业","propose 求婚； 提议，建议"]},{"id":"e01p0304","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle was touched when tears welled up in his eyes.","r":true,"m":["be touched 被感动","well up 涌出"]},{"id":"e01p0305","s":"Alice","t":"But she soon discovered this happened every time Carlos closed a big deal.","r":true,"m":["close a deal 达成交易"]},{"id":"e01p0306","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle liked her paella piping hot.","r":true,"m":["piping hot 滚烫的 piping 管道系统；尖声；笛声"]},{"id":"e01p0307","s":"Alice","t":"However, her relationship with her husband was considerably cooler.","r":true,"m":["considerably 非常，相当多地"]},{"id":"e01p0308","s":"Carlos","t":"If you talk to Al Mason at this thing, I want you to casually mention how much I paid for your necklace.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0309","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Why don't I just pin the receipt to my chest?","r":true,"m":["pin 钉住，别住; 别针，大头针","receipt 发票，收据; 收到，接收","chest 胸部，胸膛  pin the receipt to my chest"]},{"id":"e01p0310","s":"Carlos","t":"He let me know how much he paid for his wife's new convertible.","r":true,"m":["convertible 活动顶篷式汽车；可换证券；可转换的，可兑换的"]},{"id":"e01p0311","s":"Carlos","t":"Look, just work it into the conversation.","r":true,"m":["work it into the conversation. 把它融入谈话中。","work into 添加，包含; 混合，搅拌; 逐渐使处于"]},{"id":"e01p0312","s":"Gabrielle","t":"There's no way I can just work that in, Carlos.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0313","s":"Carlos","t":"Why not? At the Donahue party, everyone was talking mutual funds. And you found a way to mention you slept with half the Yankee outfield.","r":true,"m":["mutual funds 共同基金","Yankee 美国佬，美国人；洋基队（美国棒球队名）","outfield 外场；边境；偏远的田园"]},{"id":"e01p0314","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I'm telling you, it came up in the context of the conversation.","r":true,"m":["I'm telling you 我告诉你：表示强调，用于向对方强调某个观点或事实。","come up 提出，想出; 接近，靠近;升职，晋升;发生，出现;失败，没有结果","in the context of 在…背景下；在…情境中","in the context of the conversation 在对话的上下文中"]},{"id":"e01p0315","s":"Carlos","t":"Hey, people are starting to stare. Can you keep your voice down, please?","r":true,"m":["stare 凝视，盯着看"]},{"id":"e01p0316","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Absolutely, we wouldn't want them to think we're not happy.","r":true}]},{"id":"p04","title":"Bree 出场","lines":[{"id":"e01p0401","s":"Alice","t":"Bree Van De Kamp, who lives next door, brought baskets of muffins she baked from scratch.","r":true,"m":["next door 隔壁","basket 篮子","muffin 小松糕；英国松饼","bake from scratch 从头开始烘焙：指食品完全从基础原料开始制作，而不是使用预先制作好的混合物或面团。bake 烤，烘，焙；炎热，灼热；炙烤，受晒","scratch v./n. 挠，轻抓；划痕，划伤；from scratch 从零开始"]},{"id":"e01p0402","s":"Alice","t":"Bree was known for her cooking.","r":true,"m":["be known for 因……而众所周知"]},{"id":"e01p0403","s":"Alice","t":"And for making her own clothes.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0404","s":"Alice","t":"And for doing her own gardening.","r":true,"m":["do the gardening 做园艺"]},{"id":"e01p0405","s":"Alice","t":"And for reupholstering her own furniture.","r":true,"m":["reupholstering furniture 翻新家具 reupholster 重装椅面"]},{"id":"e01p0406","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, Bree's many talents were known throughout the neighborhood.","r":true,"m":["throughout prep./adv. 遍及，到处；自始至终，贯穿整个时期"]},{"id":"e01p0407","s":"Alice","t":"And everyone on Wisteria Lane thought of Bree as the perfect wife and mother.","r":true,"m":["think of sb as 把某人看作是……；认为某人是……"]},{"id":"e01p0408","s":"Alice","t":"Everyone, that is, except her own family.","r":true,"m":["that is 即；就是说；换言之"]},{"id":"e01p0409","s":"Paul","t":"Bree, you shouldn't have gone to all this trouble.","r":true,"m":["you shouldn’t have gone to all this trouble. 你本不该费这么大周折的","回答：It was no trouble at all. 这根本不麻烦","shouldn't have + 过去分词结构用于表示过去本不应该做某事，但实际上做了","完整标准短语：go to the trouble (of doing sth) 做额外的工作"]},{"id":"e01p0410","s":"Bree","t":"It was no trouble at all.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0411","s":"Bree","t":"Now, the basket with the red ribbon is filled with desserts for your guests.","r":true,"m":["ribbon 丝带，绸带","be filled with 充满，装满,被……填满 == be full of"]},{"id":"e01p0412","s":"Bree","t":"But the one with the blue ribbon is just for you and Zachary.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0413","s":"Bree","t":"It's got rolls, muffins, breakfast type things.","r":true,"m":["'s got = has got = has 拥有、具有","rolls 面包卷; 滚动（roll 的复数）；捆；","breakfast type things 早餐类的东西"]},{"id":"e01p0414","s":"Bree","t":"Well, the least I could do is make sure you boys had a decent meal to look forward to in the morning.","r":true,"m":["least 最低程度地；最少，至少 一点儿；最少的","the least I could do is... 我至少能做的是……；我最起码可以做的是……","The least I could do is (to) make sure (that) you boys had a decent meal.","1. make sure前省略了to，不定式短语作表语时，如果主语部分含有实义动词（这里是do），可省略 to。","2. 从句中用had，与前面的could在时态上保持一致，这种表达是站在过去的角度，讲述过去觉得自己至少能做的事是确保孩子们吃上像样的饭。也可改成 would have.","decent 像样的，尚好的；得体的，合宜的；","look forward to 期待：对未来某事的期待和兴奋。"]},{"id":"e01p0415","s":"Bree","t":"I know you're out of your minds with grief.","r":true,"m":["out of your minds with grief. 因为悲伤而失去理智"]},{"id":"e01p0416","s":"Paul","t":"Yes, we are.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0417","s":"Bree","t":"Of course, I will need the baskets back once you're done.","r":true}]},{"id":"p05","title":"Susan 出场","lines":[{"id":"e01p0501","s":"Alice","t":"Susan Mayer, who lives across the street, brought macaroni and cheese.","r":true,"m":["across the street 在街对面或者到达街对面","macaroni 通心粉"]},{"id":"e01p0502","s":"Alice","t":"Her husband, Carl, always teased her about her macaroni, saying it was the only thing she knew how to cook and she rarely made it well.","r":true,"m":["tease 取笑，嘲笑；逗弄  tease her about her work","rarely 罕有，很少；"]},{"id":"e01p0503","s":"Alice","t":"It was too salty the night she and Carl moved into their house.","r":true,"m":["salty 咸的，含盐的"]},{"id":"e01p0504","s":"Alice","t":"It was too watery the night she found lipstick on Carl's shirt.","r":true,"m":["watery 水的；淡的；湿的；松软的","lipstick 口红，唇膏 lip 嘴唇  stick 粘，贴；"]},{"id":"e01p0505","s":"Alice","t":"She burned it the night Carl told her he was leaving her for his secretary.","r":true,"m":["burn 燃烧，消耗；烧坏，烧毁，烧焦；过去式和过去分词：burnt或burned","secretary 秘书"]},{"id":"e01p0506","s":"Alice","t":"A year had passed since the divorce.","r":true,"m":["divorce 离婚"]},{"id":"e01p0507","s":"Alice","t":"Susan had started to think how nice it would be to have a man in her life.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0508","s":"Alice","t":"Even one who would make fun of her cooking.","r":true,"m":["Even one who... 即使是一个……的人，如Even one who has a lot of experience may make mistakes","make fun of 嘲笑，取笑"]},{"id":"e01p0509","s":"Julie","t":"Mom, why would someone kill themselves?","r":true},{"id":"e01p0510","s":"Susan","t":"Well, sometimes people are so unhappy, they think that's the only way they can solve their problems.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0511","s":"Julie","t":"But Mrs. Young always seemed happy.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0512","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, sometimes people pretend to be one way on the outside when they're totally different on the inside.","r":true,"m":["pretend to be 假装是"]},{"id":"e01p0513","s":"Julie","t":"Are you meaning, like, how dad's girlfriend is always smiling, says nice things, but deep down, you just know she's a bitch.","r":true,"m":["are you meaning... 询问对方是不是在指某件事 == Do you mean(正式)","says nice things 说好听的话","deep down 实际上；在心底"]},{"id":"e01p0514","s":"Susan","t":"I don't like that word, Julie. But, yeah, that's a great example.","r":true}]},{"id":"p06","title":"主妇们讨论 Carl 出轨","lines":[{"id":"e01p0601","s":"Alice","t":"So, what did Carl say when you confronted him?","r":true,"m":["confront 面对，面临；正视，处理；对峙，对抗；对质，当面对证"]},{"id":"e01p0602","s":"Susan","t":"You'll love this. He said \"It doesn't mean anything, it was just sex.\"","r":true},{"id":"e01p0603","s":"Bree","t":"Ah, yes, page one of the philanderer's handbook.","r":true,"m":["philanderer 花花公子","handbook 手册，指南"]},{"id":"e01p0604","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, and then he got this Zen look on his face, and he said, \"You know, Susan, most men live lives of quiet desperation.\"","r":true,"m":["zen look 禅意造型：一种简约、自然、平静的外表造型  zen 禅；禅宗"]},{"id":"e01p0605","s":"Lynette","t":"Please tell me you punched him.","r":true,"m":["punch v. 用拳猛击（某人或某物）n. 一拳，一击；"]},{"id":"e01p0606","s":"Susan","t":"No, I said, \"Really? And what do most women live? lives of noisy fulfillment?\"","r":true,"m":["fulfillment n. 履行；实行；满足","lives of noisy fulfillment 充满喧嚣的满足感的生活"]},{"id":"e01p0607","s":"Alice","t":"Hmm, good for you.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0608","s":"Susan","t":"I mean, of all people, did he have to bang his secretary? I had that woman over for brunch.","r":true,"m":["bang 猛敲，砰然重击；猛摔；很响地使劲关上；与……性交；砰砰作响","have sb over for... 邀请某人过来（做某事），for后面通常接名词，说明邀请的目的"]},{"id":"e01p0609","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's like my grandmother always said, an erect penis doesn't have a conscience.","r":true,"m":["conscience 良知，良心；内疚，愧疚 have a conscience. 有良知；有良心"]},{"id":"e01p0610","s":"Lynette","t":"Even the limp ones aren't that ethical.","r":true,"m":["ethical 道德的，伦理的；合乎道德的；"]},{"id":"e01p0611","s":"Bree","t":"This is half the reason I joined the NRA. ","r":true,"m":["half the reason 一半原因；部分原因","NRA National Rifle Association 全国枪支协会 Rifle 步枪，来复枪；步枪队"]},{"id":"e01p0612","s":"Bree","t":"Well, when Rex started going to those medical conferences, I wanted it in the back of his mind that he had a loving wife at home with a loaded Smith & Wesson.","r":true,"m":["conference （大型、正式的）会议，研讨会；（小型正式的）商讨，讨论；体育协会（或联合会）","in the back of one's mind 在某人的潜意识里；在某人脑海深处","Smith & Wesson 枪支【Smith&Wesson(史密斯威森 )公司以制造手枪闻名于世，其制造生产的产品遍布各阶层】"]},{"id":"e01p0613","s":"Alice","t":"Lynnie, Tom's always away on business. Do you ever worry he might?","r":true,"m":["be away on business 出差；因公外出"]},{"id":"e01p0614","s":"Lynette","t":"Oh, please, the man's got me pregnant 3 times in 4 years. I wish he was having sex with someone else.","r":true,"m":["get sb. + adj. 使某人处于某种状态","I wish he were having ~ 是虚拟语气，美式口语可以这么表达，但标准写法是 I wish he were having ~ "]},{"id":"e01p0615","s":"Bree","t":"So, Susan, is he gonna stop seeing that woman?","r":true,"m":["gonna 即将，将要（即 going to）"]},{"id":"e01p0616","s":"Susan","t":"I don't know. I'm sorry, you guys, I just don't know how I'm gonna survive this.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0617","s":"Alice","t":"Listen to me, we all have moments of desperation.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0618","s":"Alice","t":"But if we can face them head on, that's when we find out just how strong we really are.","r":true,"m":["face them head on 直面困难  head on 迎面地"]}]},{"id":"p07","title":"主妇们 Alice 葬礼对话","lines":[{"id":"e01p0701","s":"Bree","t":"Susan, I was just saying Paul wants us to go over on Friday.","r":true,"m":["go over / have sb over 里的 over 有登门、到某人家里的意思"]},{"id":"e01p0702","s":"Bree","t":"He needs us to go through Mary Alice's closet and help pack up her things.","r":true,"m":["go through the closet 翻衣柜","pack up 收拾，整理","help (to) do sth  “帮忙做某事”。这里的 “to” 可以省略"]},{"id":"e01p0703","s":"Bree","t":"He said he can't face doing it by himself.","r":true,"m":["face doing sth 意思是 “面对 / 面临做某事” = be faced with sth"]},{"id":"e01p0704","s":"Susan","t":"If Mary Alice was having problems, she should have come to us, she should've let us help her.","r":true,"m":["If she was having problems, she should have come to us. if 条件句的虚拟, 假设过去, 从句使用了过去进行时来表示假设，主句用情态动词 should + have done","本来虚拟从句 if 后面跟过去完成时 had been having，但是在口语中，常用 was/were doing 替代"]},{"id":"e01p0705","s":"Gabrielle","t":"What kinds of problems could she have had?","r":true,"m":["What kinds of 表示 “什么样的；哪类；哪些种类的”，后面通常接可数名词的复数形式","could she have had：情态动词 could + have done，对过去曾经存在的事情进行推测","could she have：情态动词 could + 动词原形，推测当下/常态的情况；"]},{"id":"e01p0706","s":"Gabrielle","t":"She was healthy, had a great home, a nice family, her life was... Our life.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0707","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No. If Mary Alice was having some sort of crisis, we'd have known.","r":true,"m":["some sort of 某种类型的","crisis 危机，紧要关头；决定性时刻，关键时刻","we'd have known 虚拟语气 We would have known."]},{"id":"e01p0708","s":"Gabrielle","t":"She lives 50 feet away, for God's sake.","r":true,"m":["50 feet away 50 英尺远","for God's sake 看在上帝面上 sake 利益，好处；目的"]},{"id":"e01p0709","s":"Susan","t":"Gabby, the woman killed herself. Something must've been going on.","r":true,"m":["Something must've been going on 一定发生了什么事 going on 进行，发生 what's going on"]}]},{"id":"p08","title":"Susan 初遇 Mike","lines":[{"id":"e01p0801","s":"Susan","t":"I wouldn't eat that if I were you.","r":true,"m":["对现在的虚拟：if + 一般过去时（were/did）→ 主句用 would/could/might do"]},{"id":"e01p0802","s":"Susan","t":"I made it. Trust me. Hey, do you have a death wish?","r":true,"m":["Do you have a death wish? 对当下明显的危险、鲁莽行为发出质问","death wish 死亡愿望"]},{"id":"e01p0803","s":"Mike","t":"No, I just refuse to believe that anybody can screw up macaroni and cheese.","r":true,"m":["refuse to believe 不相信：拒绝相信某事或某人所说的话。","screw up 搞砸 screw 螺丝 screw it up"]},{"id":"e01p0804","s":"Mike","t":"Oh my god. How did you...? It tastes like it's burned and undercooked.","r":true,"m":["burned 烧坏的，烧伤的  burn 烧，燃烧，消耗","undercooked 煎（或烤、炸）得火候不足的；煮得欠熟的"]},{"id":"e01p0805","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, I get that a lot. Here you go.","r":true,"m":["I get that a lot 我经常听到（别人这么说）；这种情况我碰到很多次了；我常常遇到这样的事","Here you go 给你；拿去吧；递给别人东西时说"]},{"id":"e01p0806","s":"Mike","t":"Thanks, I'm Mike Delfino. I just started renting the Sims' house next door.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0807","s":"Susan","t":"Susan Mayer. I live across the street.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0808","s":"Mike","t":"Oh yeah, Mrs. Huber told me about you, said you illustrate children's books.","r":true,"m":["illustrate 加插图于；说明，阐明；illustrate a story为一个故事配图"]},{"id":"e01p0809","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, I'm very big with the under-five set. What do you do?","r":true,"m":["be big with...  “受…… 欢迎；在…… 群体中很吃得开”","the under-5 set. 五岁以下的群体(限统计、行业文本) == under the age of 5.","What do you do 你是做什么工作的"]},{"id":"e01p0810","s":"Mike","t":"Plumber. So if you ever have a clog... or something.","r":true,"m":["plumber 水管工人，水电工","clog 阻塞，堵塞"]},{"id":"e01p0811","s":"Susan","t":"Now that everybody's seen that I brought something. I should probably just throw this out.","r":true,"m":["Now that == Since 既然；由于，引导原因状语从句"]}]},{"id":"p09","title":"Lynette 葬礼泳池闹剧","lines":[{"id":"e01p0901","s":"Lynette","t":"Ease up, you little vampire.","r":true,"m":["ease up 减轻, 轻点","vampire 吸血鬼"]},{"id":"e01p0902","s":"Mrs. Huber","t":"Lynette, I've been looking all over for you. Are you aware of what your sons are doing?","r":true,"m":["all over 到处都是；遍布全身 look all over for you","Are you aware of 你是否意识到... Are you aware that"]},{"id":"e01p0903","s":"Kid","t":"Cannonball!","r":true,"m":["cannonball 炮弹"]},{"id":"e01p0904","s":"Lynette","t":"Stop! What are you doing? We are at a wake.","r":true,"m":["wake v. 唤醒，醒来；唤起，激起；守夜，为……守灵 n.（葬礼前后的）守夜，守灵；"]},{"id":"e01p0905","s":"Kid","t":"When we got here, you said we could go in the pool.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0906","s":"Lynette","t":"I said you could go by the pool. Do you have your swimsuits on?","r":true,"m":["swimsuit 游泳衣","have clothes on 表示 “穿着衣服”，强调身上有衣物穿着的状态。"]},{"id":"e01p0907","s":"Kid","t":"Yeah, we put them on under our clothes just before we left.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0908","s":"Lynette","t":"You three planned this? All right. That's it. Get out. I am your mother. You have to do what I say. Come on.","r":true,"m":["That's it 到此为止、我受够了。"]},{"id":"e01p0909","s":"Kid","t":"We wanna swim and you can't stop us!","r":true},{"id":"e01p0910","s":"Lynette","t":"Think I won't get in this pool and just grab you? Get out! Get over here.","r":true,"m":["grab 攫取，抓住；","get over here 到这里来"]},{"id":"e01p0911","s":"Lynette","t":"Paul, we have to leave now. Once again, I am so sorry for your loss.","r":true},{"id":"e01p0912","s":"Alice","t":"Lynette shouldn't have been so concerned about my husband. ","r":true,"m":["be concerned about 关心；担忧；挂念 concern v.使某人担忧"]},{"id":"e01p0913","s":"Alice","t":"He had other things on his mind. Things below the surface.","r":true,"m":["on one’s mind：有心事、发愁、放不下 have sth on one’s mind","in his mind 在某人的脑海里、在某人的思维之中","below the surface 在表面之下"]}]},{"id":"p10","title":"Julie 主动了解 Mike","lines":[{"id":"e01p1001","s":"Alice","t":"The morning after my funeral, my friends and neighbors quietly went back to their busy, busy lives.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1002","s":"Alice","t":"While some did their cooking. And some did their cleaning. And some did their yoga. Others did their \"homework\"","r":true},{"id":"e01p1003","s":"Julie","t":"Hi, I'm Julie. I kicked my soccer ball into your backyard.","r":true,"m":["kick v.踢，踢腿；","backyard 后院；后庭"]},{"id":"e01p1004","s":"Mike","t":"Oh, OK. Well, let's go around and get it.","r":true,"m":["let's go round/around and get it 咱们过去把它拿过来。go around（美式）；go round（英式）"]},{"id":"e01p1005","s":"Julie","t":"His wife died a year ago. He wanted to stay in LA, but there were too many memories. He is renting for tax purposes, but he hopes to buy a place real soon.","r":true,"m":["tax purposes 纳税目的  tax 税款；负担，重负  purposes 目的，意图；目标，计划","for other purposes 为了其他目的；for specific purposes为了特定目的","real soon 真快：表示某事将会很快发生或完成；规范书面用 really soon"]},{"id":"e01p1006","s":"Susan","t":"I can't believe you went over there.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1007","s":"Julie","t":"Hey, I saw you both flirting at the wake. You are obviously into each other. Now that you know he is single, you can ask him out.","r":true,"m":["you both = you two 你们两个","flirt 调情；不认真地考虑","you are into each other 你们喜欢对方"]},{"id":"e01p1008","s":"Susan","t":"Julie, I like Mr. Delfino, I do. I just... I don't even know if I'm ready to start dating yet.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1009","s":"Julie","t":"You need to get back out there. Come on. How long has it been since you had sex? Are you mad that I asked you that?","r":true,"m":["get back out there 重新开始；继续前进；再次尝试","How long has it been since... 自从…… 以来已经多久了,回答时通常会用类似 “It's been + 时间段”"]},{"id":"e01p1010","s":"Susan","t":"No, I'm just trying to remember. I don't wanna talk to you about my love life anymore. It weirds me out.","r":true,"m":["wanna 想要（等于 want to）","It weirds me out 让某人感到别扭、浑身不自在、毛骨悚然"]},{"id":"e01p1011","s":"Julie","t":"I wouldn't have said anything. It's just...","r":true,"m":["I wouldn't have said anything. It's just...  我本不想说什么，只是…"]},{"id":"e01p1012","s":"Susan","t":"What?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1013","s":"Julie","t":"I heard Dad's girlfriend ask if you'd dated anyone since the divorce. And Dad said he doubted it. And then they both laughed.","r":true,"m":["hear sb do sth 听见某人做某事, 其中do sth是不带 to 的不定式","Dad said he doubted it. 在间接引语中，当主句的谓语动词是过去时态（said）时，从句中的动词通常也要使用相应的过去时态来保持时态的一致性。"]}]},{"id":"p11","title":"Susan 遇劲敌 Eddie","lines":[{"id":"e01p1101","s":"Susan","t":"Hi, Mike. I brought you a little house-warming gift. I probably should've brought something by earlier, but...","r":true,"m":["bring sb sth 给某人带来某物，双宾结构 bring -> brought -> brought","house-warming gift 乔迁礼","should have done 本该做，但当时没做，现在感到遗憾","bring sth by 顺路带东西上门拜访","earlier 早些时候地"]},{"id":"e01p1102","s":"Mike","t":"Actually, you're the first neighbor who stopped by.","r":true,"m":["stop by 顺路过来拜访 ≈ stop over "]},{"id":"e01p1103","s":"Susan","t":"Really?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1104","s":"Alice","t":"Susan knew she was lucky. An eligible bachelor had moved on to Wisteria Lane, and she was the first to find out.","r":true,"m":["eligible 符合条件的，合格的；（婚姻）合适的，合意的","bachelor 未婚男子，单身汉；学士  I graduated from xxx University with a bachelor’s degree in xxx","find out 发现，查明"]},{"id":"e01p1105","s":"Alice","t":"But she also knew that good news travels quickly.","r":true,"m":["Good news travels quickly 好事传千里","Good news travels slowly, bad news travels fast. 好事不出门，坏事传千里。讲速度快慢 → fast 讲赶紧、马上做 → quickly"]},{"id":"e01p1106","s":"Eddie","t":"Hello, there.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1107","s":"Alice","t":"Eddie Britt was the most predatory divorcee in a five-block radius.","r":true,"m":["predatory adj. 捕食性的，食肉的；掠夺性的，弱肉强食的","divorcee 离了婚的人 employer 雇主 employee 雇员 -er：干这件事的人 -ee：摊上/经历这件事的人","radius 半径；半径范围，周围","in a + 数量词 + radius（of...）在…… 半径范围内；描述某个区域范围"]},{"id":"e01p1108","s":"Alice","t":"Her conquests were numerous, varied and legendary.","r":true,"m":["conquest 掠夺物 征服，占领；占领地，征服的土地；克服，攻克；爱情的俘虏","numerous 众多的，许多的","varied 各种各样的，形形色色的；多变的；杂色的","legendary 非常有名的，大名鼎鼎的；传说（中）的"]},{"id":"e01p1109","s":"Eddie","t":"I hope I'm not interrupting. You must be Mike Delfino. Hi, I'm Eddie Britt. I live over there. Welcome to Wisteria Lane.","r":true,"m":["I hope I'm not interrupting. 希望我没有打扰你们。interrupt v. 打断，打扰；使暂停；阻断","over there 方位副词短语，在那边；在那里"]},{"id":"e01p1110","s":"Alice","t":"Susan had met the enemy. And she was a slut.","r":true,"m":["enemy 敌人，反对者；敌国，敌军；大敌，危害物","slut 荡妇；懒妇；母狗"]},{"id":"e01p1111","s":"Mike","t":"Thank you. What's this?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1112","s":"Eddie","t":"Sausage puttanesca. It's just something I threw together.","r":true,"m":["Sausage puttanesca 茄汁香肠","Sausage 香肠腊肠 My mom makes the best sausages. 我妈妈做的香肠最好吃。","puttanesca 普塔内斯卡（酱），是一种源自意大利那不勒斯的经典意面酱 My Brilliant Friend 我的天才女友","throw together 快速组装，没有精度 throw -> threw -> thrown"]},{"id":"e01p1113","s":"Mike","t":"Thanks, Eddie. That's great. I'd invite you both in, but I was sort of in the middle of something.","r":true,"m":["I'd == I would 委婉表达当下情况：我本想邀请，但是此刻正有事。","invite sb in 邀请某人进来","sort of 有点儿 sorta: [美俚](=sort of)","in the middle of something 正忙着手头一件事、有事脱不开身"]},{"id":"e01p1114","s":"Susan","t":"I'm late for an appointment anyway.","r":true,"m":["be late for 做某事迟到；赶不上……","appointment 约会，约定；任命，委派；职务，职位；家具，陈设","anyway 不管怎样，无论如何；而且，加之；尽管，即使这样；对了，好吧"]},{"id":"e01p1115","s":"Eddie","t":"No problem, I just wanted to say hi.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1116","s":"Alice","t":"And just like that, the race for Mike Delfino had begun.","r":true,"m":["race n. 赛跑，速度竞赛；竞争，角逐；v. （和……）比赛，参加比赛；"]},{"id":"e01p1117","s":"Alice","t":"For a moment, Susan wondered if her rivalry with Eddie would remain friendly.","r":true,"m":["wonder v. 想知道，好奇","rivalry 竞争，较量","would 此处表示（当时内心预判）将来会不会……；could 侧重客观可能性","remain friendly 保持友好"]},{"id":"e01p1118","s":"Alice","t":"But she was reminded that when it came to men — women don't fight fair.","r":true,"m":["remind v. 提醒，使想起 remain v. 逗留，留下；剩余；保持不变","when it came to sb/sth 当涉及到……；当谈到……；一提到……，通常用于引出某个特定的话题","fight fair 公平竞争"]},{"id":"e01p1119","s":"Eddie","t":"Oh, Mike. I heard you're a plumber. Do you think you could stop by later tonight and take a look at my pipes?","r":true,"m":["take a look at sth 看一看、检查某物"]},{"id":"e01p1120","s":"Mike","t":"Sure.","r":false}]},{"id":"p12","title":"Gabrielle 和 Carlos 为晚宴争吵","lines":[{"id":"e01p1201","s":"Gabrielle","t":"You can't order me around like I am a child. No, no. I'm not going.","r":true,"m":["order around 指挥","正式写作中，like 不能引导从句，虚拟语气要用 were,标准写法：You can't order me around as if I were a child."]},{"id":"e01p1202","s":"Carlos","t":"It's business. Tanaka expects everyone to bring their wives.","r":true,"m":["expect sb to do sth  期望某人做某事"]},{"id":"e01p1203","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Every time I'm around that man, he tries to grab my ass.","r":true,"m":["be around sb 在某人身边；在某人周围；","grab v. 攫取，抓住；"]},{"id":"e01p1204","s":"Carlos","t":"I made over $200,000 doing business with him last year. If he wants to grab your ass, you let him.","r":true,"m":["do business with 与……做生意","200,000 two hundred thousand","make money doing sth 通过做某事赚钱。 doing sth 是现在分词短作方式状语，用来表示赚钱的方式。"]},{"id":"e01p1205","s":"Carlos","t":"John!","r":false},{"id":"e01p1206","s":"John","t":"Mr. Solis, you scared me.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1207","s":"Carlos","t":"Why is that bush still there? You were supposed to dig it up last week.","r":true,"m":["bush 灌木，灌木丛；","be supposed to 被期望做某事;应该做某事","dig up 挖掘，发掘"]},{"id":"e01p1208","s":"John","t":"I didn't have time last week.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1209","s":"Carlos","t":"I don't want to hear your excuses. Just take care of it.","r":true,"m":["excuse n. 借口，托词；正当理由","take care of 处理、办妥、搞定（任务、麻烦、事务），这里不是照顾照料的意思","take care of it it 指代前面 dig up the bush 这件事"]},{"id":"e01p1210","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I really hate the way you talk to me.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1211","s":"Carlos","t":"And I really hate that I spent $15,000 on your diamond necklace that you couldn’t live without.","r":true,"m":["花钱固定用 spend money on sth 花时间一般用 spend time (in) doing sth","diamond 钻石","couldn’t live without 没有…… 就无法生活"]},{"id":"e01p1212","s":"Carlos","t":" But I'm learning to deal with it. So, can I tell Tanaka we'll be there tomorrow night?","r":true,"m":["deal with 处理，解决"]},{"id":"e01p1213","s":"Gabrielle","t":"John, we have bandages, top shelf in the kitchen.","r":true,"m":["bandage 绷带","top shelf 顶级货架top shelf in the kitchen 厨房的顶层架子"]},{"id":"e01p1214","s":"John","t":"Thanks, Mrs. Solis.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1215","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Fine, I'll go. But I'm keeping my back pressed against the wall the entire time.","r":true,"m":["press against 紧贴，压在……上","keep + 宾语 + 宾语补足语: 使…… 保持（某种状态）pressed 过去分词作宾语补足语，用于补充说明宾语 “my back” 所处的状态。过去分词作宾语补足语常用来表示被动或完成的意义，在这里后背是被外力（自身的行为或者其他客观因素等）压在墙上的，所以用过去分词形式很合适。","the entire time 整个期间；自始至终 == all the time"]},{"id":"e01p1216","s":"Carlos","t":"See, now this is what a marriage is all about. Compromise.","r":true,"m":["all about 关于一切","This is what ... is all about 这就是…… 的全部内涵；这就是…… 的意义所在；这就是…… 的关键之处","Compromise 折中，妥协；"]},{"id":"e01p1217","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Is your finger OK?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1218","s":"John","t":"Yeah, it's just a small cut.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1219","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Let me see. Mm.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1220","s":"John","t":"You know, Mrs. Solis, I really like it when we hook up, but you know, I gotta get my work done and I can't afford to lose this job.","r":true,"m":["hook up 连接 搭讪 这里表示（私下）约会 hook 钩住，挂住","gotta == got to 必须，不得不","get sth done 使某事被做；让某事得以完成","afford 买得起；有（时间）做某事；承担得起；"]},{"id":"e01p1221","s":"Gabrielle","t":"This table was hand-carved. Carlos had it imported from Italy. It cost him $23,000.","r":true,"m":["hand-carved 手工雕刻的","cost → cost → cost 花费","have sth imported from somewhere 让某物从某地进口；使某物从某地被进口"]},{"id":"e01p1222","s":"John","t":"You want to do it on the table this time?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1223","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Absolutely.","r":false}]},{"id":"p13","title":"Bree 一家的晚餐","lines":[{"id":"e01p1301","s":"Danielle","t":"Why can't we ever have normal soup?","r":true,"m":["否定词 + ever，强化 “从来都不、每次都不”，带吐槽情绪"]},{"id":"e01p1302","s":"Bree","t":"Danielle, there is nothing abnormal about basil puree.","r":true,"m":["abnormal adj. 反常的，异常的","basil puree 罗勒汤  basil 罗勒属植物,九层塔 mint 薄荷 puree 浓汤；果泥；菜泥"]},{"id":"e01p1303","s":"Danielle","t":"Just once, couldn't we have a soup that people have heard of? Like French onion or navy bean.","r":true,"m":["couldn't we do sth?  我们难道不能做某事吗？","hear of 知道，了解","French onion soup 法式洋葱汤","navy bean 白芸豆 navy 海军；深蓝色；舰队"]},{"id":"e01p1304","s":"Bree","t":"First of all, your father can't eat onions. He's deathly allergic. And I won't even dignify your navy bean suggestion. So, how's the Ossobuco?","r":true,"m":["deathly 致命的，极其，非常","allergic 对……过敏的；过敏引起的，过敏性的；对……极其反感的","dignify 使有尊严，使高贵；使显得堂皇，抬高……的身价","I won’t dignify sth (with a reply/response) 完整用法:我才懒得搭理这件事，这件事太荒唐 / 离谱，根本不配我认真回应。","Ossobuco 经典的意大利菜肴，烩牛膝或炖小牛膝"]},{"id":"e01p1305","s":"Andrew","t":"It's OK.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1306","s":"Bree","t":"It's OK? Andrew, I spent 3 hours cooking this meal. How do you think it makes me feel when you say \"it's OK\" in that sullen tone?","r":true,"m":["How do you think it makes me feel when... 你认为当…的时候，这让我有怎样的感受？","in that sullen tone 用那种闷闷不乐的/阴沉的语气","sullen 愠怒的，不高兴的；（天气）阴沉的；沉闷的","tone 语气，腔调，口吻；气氛，基调，风格"]},{"id":"e01p1307","s":"Andrew","t":"Who asked you to spend 3 hours on dinner?","r":true,"m":["who asked you to do sth? 谁让你做某事的？"]},{"id":"e01p1308","s":"Bree","t":"Excuse me?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1309","s":"Andrew","t":"Tim Harper's mom gets home from work, pops open a can of pork and beans, and boom, they're eating, everyone's happy.","r":true,"m":["get home 回家 get home from work 下班回家","pops 模拟 “砰” 一声的短促爆破动作 pop open sth 猛地一下撬开 / 掀开","boom 习惯用法：紧接着、转眼、一下子就","pork and beans 猪肉豆 pork 猪肉"]},{"id":"e01p1310","s":"Bree","t":"You'd rather I serve pork and beans?","r":true,"m":["would rather + 从句 从句动词一律用一般过去式（虚拟）所以标准表达是You'd rather I served pork and beans? 但是口语可以弱化虚拟规则，直接用动词原形 serve","would rather do sth 宁愿做…"]},{"id":"e01p1311","s":"Danielle","t":"Apologize now. I am begging.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1312","s":"Andrew","t":"I'm saying, do you always have to serve cuisine? Can't we ever just have food?","r":true,"m":["cuisine 这里指经过精心准备、具有特定烹饪风格或特色的菜肴"]},{"id":"e01p1313","s":"Bree","t":"Are you doing drugs?","r":true,"m":["Are you doing drugs? 你在吸毒吗？ do drugs 吸食毒品 drug sb 给某人下药"]},{"id":"e01p1314","s":"Andrew","t":"What?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1315","s":"Bree","t":"Change in behavior is one of the warning signs, and you have been as fresh as paint for the last six months.","r":true,"m":["as fresh as paint 精神头十足、精力旺盛、状态亢奋  paint 油漆，涂料；绘画颜料"]},{"id":"e01p1316","s":"Bree","t":"That certainly would explain why you're always locked in the bathroom.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1317","s":"Danielle","t":"Trust me, that is not what he is doing.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1318","s":"Andrew","t":"Shut up. Mom, I'm not the one with the problem here, alright? You're the one always acting like she's running for mayor of Stepford.","r":true,"m":["You’re the one doing sth 你才是那个正在做某事的人 == you’re the one who is doing sth","run for 参选，寻求，逃离","mayor 镇长，市长","Stepford 地名：斯特福德市"]},{"id":"e01p1319","s":"Bree","t":"Rex, Seeing as you're the head of this household, I would really appreciate you saying something.","r":true,"m":["Seeing as 既然，鉴于","the head of this household 一家之主","household 家庭，一家人；家务；王室","appreciate 欣赏，鉴赏；理解，明白；感谢，感激；升值，增值","would appreciate sb doing sth 希望某人做某事；会感激某人做某事","I would really appreciate you saying something. == I would really appreciate it if you said something."]},{"id":"e01p1320","s":"Rex","t":"Pass the salt?","r":true}]},{"id":"p14","title":"Lynette 偶遇前同事","lines":[{"id":"e01p1401","s":"Alice","t":"Three days after my funeral, Lynette replaced her grief with a much more useful emotion - Indignation.","r":true,"m":["replace sth with sth 用…… 替换……；以…… 取代……","much + 比较级 much 用来加深比较程度，翻译：… 得多","indignation 愤愤不平，义愤；和 dignity 同词根（尊严）表示尊严受损而生的愤慨"]},{"id":"e01p1402","s":"Lynette","t":"Tom, this is my fifth message and you still haven't called me back. Well, you must be having a lot of fun on your business trip, I can only imagine.","r":true,"m":["吐槽对方到此刻还没回电话 → 只用：haven't called","I can only imagine 我只能想象；我只能设想"]},{"id":"e01p1403","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, guess what? The kids and I want to have some fun, too. So unless you call me back by noon, we are getting on a plane and joining you.","r":true,"m":["guess what? 猜猜看；你猜怎么着","by noon 到中午之前","get on a plane 登上飞机；上飞机"]},{"id":"e01p1404","s":"Lynette","t":"Not now, honey. Mommy's threatening Daddy. Where are your brothers?","r":true,"m":["threaten v. 威胁，恐吓；危及"]},{"id":"e01p1405","s":"Klein","t":"Lynette Scavo?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1406","s":"Lynette","t":"Crap. Natalie Klein. I don't believe it.","r":true,"m":["crap 糟了、完蛋了,胡扯，废话；蹩脚货，废物；"]},{"id":"e01p1407","s":"Klein","t":"Lynette. How long has it been?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1408","s":"Lynette","t":"Years. How are you? How's the firm?","r":true,"m":["firm 公司，商行；"]},{"id":"e01p1409","s":"Klein","t":"Good. Everyone misses you. We all say if you hadn't quit, you'd be running the place by now.","r":true,"m":["be running the place 管理这个地方"]},{"id":"e01p1410","s":"Klein","t":"So, how's domestic life? Don't you just love being a mom?","r":true,"m":["domestic 家用的，家庭的； 国内的，本国的；","Don’t you …? 否定反问,这里表示有预设，默认对方认同"]},{"id":"e01p1411","s":"Alice","t":"And there it was, the question that Lynette always dreaded.","r":true,"m":["dread 畏惧，担心；比 be afraid of 更严重"]},{"id":"e01p1412","s":"Alice","t":"For those who asked it, only one answer was acceptable. So Lynette responded as she always did. She lied.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1413","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, to be honest, it's the best job I've ever had.","r":true,"m":["to be honest 老实说；说实话","It's the best job I've ever had. 这是我做过的最好的工作。"]}]},{"id":"p15","title":"Gabrielle 出轨 John","lines":[{"id":"e01p1501","s":"John","t":"You know what I don't get?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1502","s":"Gabrielle","t":"What?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1503","s":"John","t":"Why you married Mr. Solis.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1504","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, he promised to give me everything I've ever wanted.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1505","s":"John","t":"And did he?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1506","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yes.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1507","s":"John","t":"Then why aren't you happy?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1508","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Turns out I wanted all the wrong things.","r":true,"m":["Turns out 结果是，原来是这样"]},{"id":"e01p1509","s":"John","t":"So do you love him?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1510","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I do.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1511","s":"John","t":"Well, then, why are we here? Why are we doing this?","r":false},{"id":"e01p1512","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Because I don't wanna wake up one morning with a sudden urge to blow my brains out.","r":true,"m":["one morning 某一天早晨；有一天早上","urge 强烈的欲望，冲动；推动力；敦促，催促，力劝","blow 猛击，打击","blow my brains out 打爆我的头"]},{"id":"e01p1513","s":"John","t":"Hey, can I have a drag?","r":true,"m":["have a drag 比较口语化的短语，抽一口（烟）","drag v. 拖，拽；生拉硬拽，强迫；费劲地移动；拖沓；用鼠标拖动"]},{"id":"e01p1514","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Absolutely not. You are much too young to smoke.","r":true,"m":["Absolutely not 绝对不；当然不；绝不"]}]},{"id":"p16","title":"Susan 再约 Mike","lines":[{"id":"e01p1601","s":"Susan","t":"How would you feel about me using your child support payments for plastic surgery?","r":true,"m":["How would you feel about sb doing sth 询问某人对其他人做某事的感受看法","use sth for sth 使用某物来做某事；把某物用于某事","child support payments 儿童抚养费","plastic surgery 整形外科","plastic 塑料制的；人造的，不自然的； 塑料","surgery 外科手术"]},{"id":"e01p1602","s":"Julie","t":"Stop being so nervous. You're just asking him out to dinner. It's no big deal.","r":true,"m":["Stop being so nervous 别那么紧张了，是一个常用的祈使句，用于劝慰、安抚他人 ==  Don't be so nervous  nervous 神经紧张的，担忧的","It's no big deal 没什么大不了的；没关系；小事一桩"]},{"id":"e01p1603","s":"Susan","t":"You're right. So is that your project for school? You know, when I was in fifth grade, I made the White House out of sugar cubes.","r":true,"m":["in fifth grade 五年级","make sth out of sth 用…… 制作……；从…… 中制造出……","sugar cube 糖块"]},{"id":"e01p1604","s":"Julie","t":"Stop stalling and go. Before Mike figures out he can do better.","r":true,"m":["Stop stalling and go 别磨蹭了，走吧","stall v. 熄火，抛锚；故意拖延；暂缓，搁置，停顿； n.货摊，贩卖处，咨询台；","figure out 弄清楚，弄明白"]},{"id":"e01p1605","s":"Susan","t":"Tell me again why I fought for custody of you.","r":true,"m":["fight for 为……而战，而奋斗","custody 监护，监护权；监禁，拘留；保管，保护"]},{"id":"e01p1606","s":"Julie","t":"You were using me to hurt Dad.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1607","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, that's right.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1608","s":"Susan","t":"Are you busy?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1609","s":"Mike","t":"No, not at all. What's up?","r":true,"m":["What's up? <非正式>你好，出了什么事"]},{"id":"e01p1610","s":"Susan","t":"Well, I just was wondering if there was any chance that you... I just wanted to ask if... Eddie. What are you...?","r":true,"m":["I was wondering if there was any chance that 询问是否有机会做某事等"]},{"id":"e01p1611","s":"Eddie","t":"I was making ambrosia, and I made too much so I thought I'd bring some over to Mike. What's going on?","r":true,"m":["ambrosia 特别美味的食物；美式语境特指一种水果奶油甜品","I thought I'd... = I thought I would...我原打算 / 我当时会……","bring some over to sb 带些…给某人","What's going on? 发生了什么：用于询问当前的情况或事件。"]},{"id":"e01p1612","s":"Mike","t":"Susan was just going to ask me something.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1613","s":"Susan","t":"I have a clog. And you're a plumber, right? The clog's in the pipe.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1614","s":"Mike","t":"Yeah. That's usually where they are.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1615","s":"Susan","t":"Well, I've got one.","r":true,"m":["I've got one 我有一个"]},{"id":"e01p1616","s":"Mike","t":"OK, let me get my tools.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1617","s":"Susan","t":"Now? You want to come over now? You have company.","r":true,"m":["come over 过来：指随意拜访或到访。","company 陪伴，同伴；宾客  公司","You have company 你有客人了 / 有人陪你了 / 家里来客人了"]},{"id":"e01p1618","s":"Eddie","t":"I don't mind.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1619","s":"Mike","t":"Just give me two minutes. I'll be right over.","r":true,"m":["I’ll be right there. （我马上就到那里。）—— 侧重于到达那个地点。","I’ll be right over. （我马上就过去。）—— 侧重于移动的动作","I’m on my way. （我在路上了。）"]},{"id":"e01p1620","s":"Susan","t":"That's it. Just stuff the hair down there.","r":true,"m":["That's it. 就是这样；正是如此 / 够了；行了 / 完成了；结束了","stuff v. 塞进，填进；填满，装满 n. 东西，物品"]},{"id":"e01p1621","s":"Julie","t":"I stuffed it. It's not enough to clog it.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1622","s":"Susan","t":"Here, look, Put in this peanut butter and this cooking oil. And these olives.","r":true,"m":["peanut butter 花生酱 peanut 花生，花生米 butter 黄油，牛油；水果酱"]},{"id":"e01p1623","s":"Julie","t":"Mom, I'm telling you, it's not working.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1624","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, god. That's him. How am I going to stop up the sink?","r":true,"m":["How am I going to do sth 我该怎么样去做...","stop up the sink 堵住水槽 sink n.水槽，水池 v.下沉，沉没；stop up 表示堵塞（管道、洞口）"]},{"id":"e01p1625","s":"Mike","t":"Well, here's your problem. Looks like somebody stuffed a bunch of popsicle sticks down here.","r":true,"m":["a bunch of 一束；一串","popsicle 棒冰","stick n. 枯枝，枝条；条状物，棍状物 v.粘，贴；刺，戳，插；"]},{"id":"e01p1626","s":"Susan","t":"I've told Julie a million times not to play in the kitchen. Kids, you know.","r":true,"m":["a million times 一百万次"]}]},{"id":"p17","title":"Rex 提出离婚","lines":[{"id":"e01p1701","s":"waiter","t":"All right, I'll go put in your orders, and I'll be right back with your drinks and your plates for the salad bar.","r":true,"m":["alright: [俚]=all right 好的","I'll go put in your orders 我去给你点餐 go + 动词原形 是美语高频口语结构，表去做某事。put in your orders 餐厅固定短语：下单、提交点餐单。","I'll be right back 我马上回来：表示暂时离开，很快就会回来。","plate n. 盘，碟；一盘（食物）；"]},{"id":"e01p1702","s":"Bree","t":"Andrew, Danielle, napkins?","r":true,"m":["napkin 餐巾纸"]},{"id":"e01p1703","s":"Andrew","t":"They have video games. Could we go play until our food gets here?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1704","s":"Bree","t":"Andrew, this is family time.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1705","s":"Rex","t":"Go ahead and play.","r":true,"m":["go ahead 前进，继续,尽管去、去吧"]},{"id":"e01p1706","s":"Bree","t":"I know that you think I'm angry about coming here, but I'm not.","r":true,"m":["be angry about doing sth对做某事感到生气 == be mad at doing sth"]},{"id":"e01p1707","s":"Bree","t":"You and the kids wanted a change of pace, something fun, I get it.","r":true,"m":["a change of pace 改变步调：改变日常生活或工作，尝试新事物避免单调乏味"]},{"id":"e01p1708","s":"Bree","t":"Probably we'll want something healthier tomorrow night, though. I'm thinking about chicken saltimbocca.","r":true,"m":["Saltimbocca 意式煎小牛肉火腿卷"]},{"id":"e01p1709","s":"Rex","t":"I want a divorce. I just can't live in this detergent commercial anymore.","r":true,"m":["detergent 洗涤剂，去污剂","commercial 商业的，商务的；","detergent commercial 清洁剂广告，这是一种隐喻，广告里是刻意表演出来、虚假完美的家庭生活"]},{"id":"e01p1710","s":"waiter","t":"The salad bar's right over there. Help yourself.","r":true,"m":["Help yourself 请自便"]},{"id":"e01p1711","s":"Bree","t":"Um, I think I'll go get your salad for you.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1712","s":"Huber","t":"Bree Van De Kamp.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1713","s":"Bree","t":"Oh. Hello, Mrs. Huber.","r":false},{"id":"e01p1714","s":"Huber","t":"We didn't get a chance to talk at Mary Alice's wake. How are you doing?","r":true,"m":["get a chance to do sth 得到一个做某事的机会"]},{"id":"e01p1715","s":"Alice","t":"Bree longed to share the truth about her husband's painful betrayal, but sadly for Bree, admitting defeat was not an option.","r":true,"m":["long to 渴望","betrayal n.背叛，出卖","admit （勉强）承认；招认，招供；准许进入（某处）；接纳，接收","defeat v./n.失败，战败；战胜，击败"]},{"id":"e01p1716","s":"Bree","t":"Great. Everything is just great.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1717","s":"Bree","t":"Ok, well, I got you the honey mustard dressing. The ranch looked just a little bit suspect.","r":true,"m":["honey mustard dressing 蜂蜜芥末酱 mustard n.芥末酱；芥末黄，深黄色 dressing n.（拌制色拉用的）调料；馅，填料 Tomato dressing番茄调味酱","ranch 大农场，大牧场 ranch dressing 牧场沙拉酱","a little bit 稍微；一点点；少量 = a little","suspect adj.不可靠的，不可信的 v.猜想，认为 n. 嫌疑犯，可疑分子","The ranch looked just a little bit suspect. 这个田园酱看起来有点不新鲜了"]},{"id":"e01p1718","s":"Rex","t":"Are we going to talk about what I said?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1719","s":"Bree","t":"If you think I'm going to discuss the dissolution of my marriage in a place where the restrooms are labeled \"chicks\" and \"dudes\", you're out of your mind.","r":true,"m":["dissolution 分解，溶解；（议会等的）解散；","in a place where ... 定语从句，对a place 进行限定和描述，说明是怎样的地方","chicks 雏鸟，小鸡；少女，小妞儿 dudes 家伙，小子","you're out of your mind 你疯了"]},{"id":"e01p1720","s":"Rex","t":"What's in this?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1721","s":"Bree","t":"What do you mean, What's in this? It's salad.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1722","s":"Rex","t":"With onion. You put onion in my salad.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1723","s":"Bree","t":"No, I didn't. Oh wait…","r":false}]},{"id":"p18","title":"Tom 回家","lines":[{"id":"e01p1801","s":"Alice","t":"The sound that awakened my son was something he'd heard only once before. Many years ago when he was quite young.","r":true,"m":["awakened awaken 的过去式及过去分词 vt. 唤醒；唤起；使……意识到  vi. 觉醒；醒来；意识到(偏书面) = woke wake的过去式及过去分词(偏口语)"]},{"id":"e01p1802","s":"Alice","t":"But he recognized it instantly. It was the sound of a family secret.","r":true,"m":["instantly adv. 立刻，马上"]},{"id":"e01p1803","s":"Alice","t":"7 days after my funeral, life on Wisteria Lane finally returned to normal, which, for some of my friends, was unfortunate.","r":true,"m":["unfortunate adj. 不幸的；令人遗憾的；不成功的","Life returned to normal, which, for some of my friends, was unfortunate. 这里用which不用that是因为后面是一个非限定性定语从句。非限定性定语从句中，有一种特殊情况，which可以指代前面整个主句而不只是前面一个名词。","对我的一些朋友来说，紫藤巷生活恢复正常这件事是不幸的。"]},{"id":"e01p1804","s":"Lynette","t":"Now what?","r":true,"m":["Now what? 又怎么了"]},{"id":"e01p1805","s":"son","t":"Daddy's home!","r":true},{"id":"e01p1806","s":"Tom","t":"Come on! Hey, is anybody home?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1807","s":"Lynette","t":"I wasn't expecting you for a week.","r":true,"m":["I wasn't expecting you 我没料到你会来；我没想到是你","I wasn't expecting you for a week. 我原本以为这一周内你都不会来；我已经快要不指望你了。"]},{"id":"e01p1808","s":"Tom","t":"I have to go back to Frisco in the morning. But I got your call. You sounded a little frazzled.","r":true,"m":["Frisco 弗里斯科（美国西部城市）","frazzled adj. 疲惫的 frazzle n. 疲惫，精疲力竭；烫皱，煮烂；烧尽 v. 使…疲惫不堪；使…被烫皱"]},{"id":"e01p1809","s":"Lynette","t":"Yeah! It's been a little rough.","r":true,"m":["It's been a little rough. 这段时间有点艰难；情况有点棘手","rough adj. （表面）粗糙的，不平的；艰难的，不愉快的；"]},{"id":"e01p1810","s":"Tom","t":"Hi, Yeah, Peaches.","r":true,"m":["Peach n. 桃子；桃树；桃红色"]},{"id":"e01p1811","s":"son","t":"Daddy, Did you buy us any presents?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1812","s":"Tom","t":"Oh, god, presents. Wait up. Let me see.","r":true,"m":["Wait up 等一下：指稍等片刻，不要离开或继续前进。"]},{"id":"e01p1813","s":"Tom","t":"But I'm not giving it to you unless you promise me to go outside right now and practise throwing for 20 minutes, okay? You promise?","r":true},{"id":"e01p1814","s":"Tom","t":"Get out! Who's open? Go out. Deeper. Deeper. Touchdown!","r":true,"m":["Deeper. Deeper. Touchdown! 远点.远点!接着! touchdown: 达阵得分，降落, 着陆"]},{"id":"e01p1815","s":"Lynette","t":"You gotta be kidding. I'm exhausted. I look terrible. I'm covered in peaches.","r":true,"m":["You gotta be kidding. 你一定是在开玩笑","I'm exhausted. 我筋疲力尽了；我累坏了"]},{"id":"e01p1816","s":"Tom","t":"I'm sorry, baby, I gotta have you.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1817","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, is it okay if I just lie here?","r":true,"m":["is it ok if I do sth 我做…… 可以吗？ 用于礼貌地征求对方的意见","lie ->lay -> lain 躺；平放；位于 lie ->lied -> lied 说谎"]},{"id":"e01p1818","s":"Tom","t":"Absolutely.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1819","s":"Lynette","t":"Wait. I gotta tell you I was having trouble with swelling. So the doctor took me off the pill. You just gotta put on a condom.","r":true,"m":["have trouble with: 有病痛","swell v. （身体部位）肿胀，膨胀","take sb. off sth.常用搭配，使某人停止服用（药物等）","pill 药片，药丸；（女用）口服避孕药 （the pill）","The doctor took me off the pill 医生让我停止服用避孕药（或那种药丸）","condom 安全套，避孕套"]},{"id":"e01p1820","s":"Tom","t":"A condom? What's the big deal? Let's risk it.","r":true,"m":["What's the big deal? 有什么大不了的"]},{"id":"e01p1821","s":"Lynette","t":"Let's risk it?","r":true}]},{"id":"p19","title":"Rex 在医院抱怨 Bree","lines":[{"id":"e01p1901","s":"Rex","t":"I can't believe you tried to kill me.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1902","s":"Bree","t":"Yes, well, I feel bad about that. I told you, Mrs. Huber came over and I got distracted. It was a mistake.","r":true,"m":["I feel bad about that. 我对此感到很难过","distract v. 使分心，使转移注意力 distracted adj. 注意力分散的，心烦意乱的"]},{"id":"e01p1903","s":"Rex","t":"Since when do you make mistakes?","r":true,"m":["since when 从什么时候开始"]},{"id":"e01p1904","s":"Bree","t":"What's that supposed to mean?","r":true,"m":["what's that supposed to mean 你这话到底什么意思？那是什么意思 suppose v.推断，料想，猜想；假设，假定，设想；预期，需要 be supposed to应该"]},{"id":"e01p1905","s":"Rex","t":"It means I'm sick of you being so damn perfect all the time.","r":true,"m":["sick of 厌倦 sick of sb doing sth（对某人做某事感到厌烦） Sick of sth（对某事感到厌烦）","damn 该死，见鬼","all the time 一直，始终"]},{"id":"e01p1906","s":"Rex","t":"I'm sick of the bizarre way your hair doesn't move.","r":true,"m":["bizarre adj.奇异的，古怪的"]},{"id":"e01p1907","s":"Rex","t":"I'm sick of you making our bed in the morning before I've even used the bathroom.","r":true,"m":["make bed 整理床铺","before 从句里，现在完成时可以强调：截止到主句动作发生时，从句动作还没有完成。","use the bathroom. 上厕所"]},{"id":"e01p1908","s":"Rex","t":"You're the plastic suburban housewife with her pearls and spatula, who says things like \"we owe the Hendersons a dinner.\"","r":true,"m":["你就像一个人造的乡村主妇，带着珍珠拿着抹刀，然后说着：“我们欠亨德森一家一顿饭。","姓氏复数一家人标准写法 the Hendersons","plastic n.塑料；信用卡；adj.塑料制的；人造的，不自然的；可塑的","suburban adj.郊区的，城郊的；平淡乏味的，乡气的，平庸的","pearl n.珍珠","spatula n.（调和、涂抹用）抹刀，小铲","owe v.欠（钱），负账；应该做，应给予；欠（人情）；归因于，归功于"]},{"id":"e01p1909","s":"Rex","t":"Where's the woman I fell in love with. Who used to burn the toast and drink milk out of the carton? and laugh?","r":true,"m":["burn the toast 把吐司烤焦 toast n.烤面包片，吐司；干杯，祝酒，敬酒","carton n.硬纸盒，塑料盒，特指装牛奶、果汁那种比较薄的盒子 Drink milk out of the carton. cardboard n. 硬纸板，纸板箱"]},{"id":"e01p1910","s":"Rex","t":"I need her, not this cold, perfect thing you've become.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1911","s":"Bree","t":"These need water.","r":true},{"id":"e01p1912","s":"Alice","t":"Bree sobbed quietly in the restroom for five minutes, but her husband never knew.","r":true,"m":["sob v. 啜泣，抽噎；哭诉"]},{"id":"e01p1913","s":"Alice","t":"Because when Bree finally emerged, she was perfect.","r":true,"m":["emerge v. 浮现，出现；显露，知悉；恢复过来；形成"]}]},{"id":"p20","title":"Gabrielle 和 Carlos 参加晚宴","lines":[{"id":"e01p2001","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I found my earrings. We can go now.","r":true,"m":["earring n. 耳环，耳饰"]},{"id":"e01p2002","s":"Carlos","t":"Was John here today?","r":true},{"id":"e01p2003","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, yeah.","r":false},{"id":"e01p2004","s":"Carlos","t":"The lawn hasn't been mowed. I've had it. We're getting a real gardener.","r":true,"m":["lawn n. 草坪，草地","mow v. 刈，割（草）","I've had it 我受够了"]},{"id":"e01p2005","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Why?","r":false},{"id":"e01p2006","s":"Carlos","t":"Are you deaf? I just said he's not doing his job.","r":true,"m":["deaf adj.聋的；置若罔闻的"]},{"id":"e01p2007","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's dark. You just can't see that the lawn has been mowed.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2008","s":"Carlos","t":"It hasn't been. Feel this grass.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2009","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I'm not feeling the grass. Let's just get going. Come on, we're late.","r":true,"m":["Let's just get going 咱们这就出发吧","Let’s just keep going. 我们继续走吧 / 继续做吧"]},{"id":"e01p2010","s":"Carlos","t":"There's Tanaka. Time for me to go into my dance.","r":true,"m":["Time for me to go into my dance. 该是我上场的时候了，我觉得可以说 Time for me to do my thing. 或者 It’s my turn. 更常用"]},{"id":"e01p2011","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Good luck, sweetheart. Excuse me. You see that man just walked away? Can you make sure he has a drink in his hand all night long.","r":true,"m":["all night long 整夜地，通宵地"]},{"id":"e01p2012","s":"valet","t":"Yes, Ma'am.","r":true,"m":["valet n. 贴身男仆；用车的人；伺候客人停车"]}]},{"id":"p21","title":"Susan 纵火","lines":[{"id":"e01p2101","s":"Susan","t":"Mrs. Huber, how are you doing?","r":true,"m":["how are you doing? 肯定回答:I'm doing well"]},{"id":"e01p2102","s":"Huber","t":"Not too well, I'm afraid. I'm trying to find something to soothe my stomach.","r":true,"m":["soothe v. 使平静，安抚；减轻，缓和（疼痛）","stomach n. 胃；腹部；"]},{"id":"e01p2103","s":"Susan","t":"It's upset?","r":true,"m":["地道标准写法应为 Is your stomach upset?"]},{"id":"e01p2104","s":"Huber","t":"Yeah. I had the worst macaroni and cheese at the wake. It's been running through me ever since.","r":true,"m":["run through me 口语固定委婉表达，特指吃完东西后持续腹泻、拉肚子；run through sb （食物）让某人腹泻","ever since 从那时起一直（强调持续到现在）","I’ve had the runs ever since. the runs = 腹泻"]},{"id":"e01p2105","s":"Huber","t":"And I need to be at my best. Eddie Britt's son is spending the night tonight.","r":true,"m":["I need to be at my best 需要处于自己的最佳状态，无论是在身体上、精神上","at one's best 指身体、精神处于最佳状态"]},{"id":"e01p2106","s":"Susan","t":"He's spending the night?","r":true},{"id":"e01p2107","s":"Huber","t":"Apparently Eddie is having a gentleman friend over for dinner. And I think she plans on entertaining into the wee hours. if you know what I mean.","r":true,"m":["apparently adv. 据说，显然；似乎，好像","have sb over for dinner 邀请某人来家里吃晚饭","plan on doing sth 计划做某事；打算做某事","plan on entertaining 计划进行娱乐活动；打算招待（某人）","into the wee hours 深夜，凌晨 wee adj.极小的；微量的 小便，排尿"]},{"id":"e01p2108","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, here's some antacid, have you ever tried this?","r":true,"m":["antacid n. 抗酸剂，解酸药"]},{"id":"e01p2109","s":"Susan","t":"I can't believe it. This can't be happening. Mike can't like Eddie better than me. He just can't.","r":true,"m":["like A better than B. = prefer A to B. 比起 B 更喜欢 A"]},{"id":"e01p2110","s":"Julie","t":"You don't know what's going on. Maybe they're just having dinner. You're right, they're doing it.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2111","s":"Susan","t":"Eddie? Hello? Anybody home? I need to borrow sugar.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2112","s":"Alice","t":"And just like that, the possibility Susan had clung to, the maybe of Mike Delfino, was gone forever.","r":true,"m":["cling -> clung v.抓住，抱紧；粘住；坚持，坚信；坚守 cling to 坚持,依附","苏珊一直坚持的可能性，迈克·德尔菲诺的可能性，永远消失了。"]},{"id":"e01p2113","s":"Alice","t":"And despite the precariousness of her situation, Susan took a moment to mourn her loss.","r":true,"m":["despite prep. 尽管，即使；Despite the rain, we went out. 尽管下雨，我们还是出去了。","precariousness n. 不安全；不稳定","the precariousness of her situation == her precarious situation","mourn v. 悼念，哀悼；对……感到痛心（遗憾）"]},{"id":"e01p2114","s":"Alice","t":"It didn't take Susan long to realize, this was just not her night.","r":true,"m":["It takes sb + 时间 + to do sth  做某事花费某人多长时间","this was just not her night. 今晚就是不属于她；她今晚诸事不顺"]},{"id":"e01p2115","s":"Eddie","t":"Is somebody out there? Oh my god! That's smoke.","r":true}]},{"id":"p22","title":"Eddie 家被火烧后","lines":[{"id":"e01p2201","s":"Huber","t":"She left candles unattended in the den. The paramedic said she was lucky. She could've been killed.","r":true,"m":["candle n. 蜡烛；旧烛光","unattended adj. 无人看管的，无人照料的；未被注意的，未被处理的； attend v. 出席；照料，照看","den n. 兽穴；窝点；活动室，休闲室","paramedic n. 护理人员","当 \"could've\" 后面紧跟一个辅音（比如 been, died, hurt）时，那个 /v/ 的音往往会被 “吃掉” 或者 “同化”，直接从 \"d\" 滑到后面的辅音。"]},{"id":"e01p2202","s":"Lynette","t":"She ran out with nothing on. She was having sex with some guy when the fire started.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2203","s":"Gabrielle","t":"What happened to him?","r":true,"m":["如果疑问词是宾语/状语，必须加 did/do/does，如 what did you see?","如果疑问词 = 动作发出者（主语）则不用加"]},{"id":"e01p2204","s":"Lynette","t":"He got smoke inhalation. He's at the hospital.","r":true,"m":["inhalation n. 吸入，吸入法；吸入剂，吸入物 smoke inhalation 烟雾吸入伤害","in the hospital（住院）at the hospital（在医院）"]},{"id":"e01p2205","s":"Bree","t":"Susan, are you all right? You look awful.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2206","s":"Susan","t":"I'm fine. I just feel really bad for Eddie.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2207","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh, honey, don't worry about Eddie. She's a strong lady.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2208","s":"Lynette","t":"Absolutely. She'll get through this. She'll find a way to survive.","r":true,"m":["get through 完成; 熬过","find a way to survive 找到生存之道；设法生存下去"]},{"id":"e01p2209","s":"Bree","t":"We all do.","r":true,"m":["We all do 我们所有人都这样做；我们全都如此"]}]},{"id":"p23","title":"火灾后 Mike 出场","lines":[{"id":"e01p2301","s":"Mike","t":"Wow! What happened?","r":true},{"id":"e01p2302","s":"Alice","t":"And suddenly there he was, like a phoenix rising from the ashes.","r":true,"m":["a phoenix rising from the ashes 凤凰浴火重生 phoenix n. 凤凰，不死鸟；rise from 起源于;从……中恢复 ash n.灰；灰烬","rise：不及物动词: 上升；升起；增加；提高；起床；起立，强调主语自身位置的上升或数量、水平等的增加，不需要借助外力。rose--risen; rising","raise：及物动词: 举起；提高；筹集；养育；饲养，强调通过外力使某物上升或使某事发生，需要有一个宾语来表示动作的对象。raised; raising"]},{"id":"e01p2303","s":"Susan","t":"Mike! I thought you were... Where were you?","r":true},{"id":"e01p2304","s":"Mike","t":"I just got back from the movies. Eddie had a fire, huh?","r":true,"m":["get back from the movies 看完电影回来"]},{"id":"e01p2305","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, but she's fine now. Everything's fine now.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2306","s":"Alice","t":"And just like that, Susan was happy. Life was suddenly full of possibilities.","r":true,"m":["be full of possibilities 充满可能性  possibility n. 可能，可能性；"]},{"id":"e01p2307","s":"Alice","t":"Not to mention a few unexpected surprises.","r":true,"m":["not to mention 更不用说、何况、此外还有","unexpected adj.想不到的，意外的"]},{"id":"e01p2308","s":"Mike","t":"It's me.","r":false},{"id":"e01p2309","s":"Man","t":"Do you have anything yet?","r":true,"m":["Do you have anything yet? 你有结果了吗？你搞定了吗？","在这种疑问句和否定句里，yet = 到现在为止。"]},{"id":"e01p2310","s":"Mike","t":" But don't worry. I'm definitely getting closer.","r":true,"m":["definitely adv. 肯定地，当然；明确地，确定地 get closer 靠近"]}]},{"id":"p24","title":"主妇们收拾 Alice 的遗物","lines":[{"id":"e01p2401","s":"Susan","t":"I brought some champagne. I thought we should have a toast.","r":true,"m":["champagne n. 香槟酒；香槟色","have a toast 举杯祝酒，更地道固定搭配：propose a toast / drink a toast"]},{"id":"e01p2402","s":"Alice","t":"The next day my friends came together to pack away my clothes, my personal belongings and what was left of my life.","r":true,"m":["pack away 收起; 存放  pack v. （把……）打包，收拾（行李）；包装，装箱；","personal belongings 个人物品"]},{"id":"e01p2403","s":"Susan","t":"All right, ladies, lift'em up. To Mary Alice, a good friend and neighbor. Wherever you are, we hope you've found peace.","r":true,"m":["lift them up 抬起他们(举杯) lift v.提起，举起；n.电梯，升降机 Raise your hand.举手"]},{"id":"e01p2404","s":"Lynette/Gabrielle/Bree","t":"To Mary Alice.","r":false},{"id":"e01p2405","s":"Lynette","t":"Let's get the show on the road.","r":true,"m":["get the show on the road 开始行动，开始进行"]},{"id":"e01p2406","s":"Gabrielle","t":"You guys, check out Mary Alice's clothes. Size 8? Ha! She always told me she was a size 6. Guess we found the skeleton in her closet.","r":true,"m":["check out 检查; 借出; 结账; 退房","be 动词：be a size + 数字; wear 动词：wear size + 数字（固定无冠词）","the skeleton in her closet 在英语中如果说某人的壁橱里有个骷髅skeleton, 意思就是这个人有难言之隐，有不可告人的家丑或秘密","Everyone has a skeleton in the closet. 每个人都有不可告人的秘密。","skeleton n. 骨骼，骨架；梗概，提纲；"]},{"id":"e01p2407","s":"Alice","t":"Not quite, Gabrielle, not quite.","r":true,"m":["not quite 不完全是；不见得：不是完全准确或符合预期，但在某种程度上接近。"]},{"id":"e01p2408","s":"Gabrielle","t":"What's that?","r":false},{"id":"e01p2409","s":"Bree","t":"It's a letter addressed to Mary Alice.","r":true,"m":["a letter addressed to 一封写给某人的信 == a letter with sb's name on it"]},{"id":"e01p2410","s":"Alice","t":"How ironic to have something I tried so desperately to keep secret treated so casually.","r":true,"m":["ironic adj. 反语的，讽刺的；How ironic. 真够讽刺的","How + 形容词 + to do（真正主语）","How ironic to have something (I tried so desperately to keep secret) treated so casually. 我拼命想要保守的秘密，却被如此随意地对待","To have something treated casually 直译：让某件事被随意对待 have sth done 某物被（别人）……；遭遇某事被怎样对待","desperately adv. 绝望地，拼命地，不顾一切地；非常，极其","casually adv. 随意地，漫不经心地；临时地；偶然地"]},{"id":"e01p2411","s":"Lynette","t":"What are you doing? That's private.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2412","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's open. What's the big deal?","r":true,"m":["What's the big deal? 有什么大不了的？"]},{"id":"e01p2413","s":"Letter","t":"I know what you did. It makes me sick. I'm going to tell.","r":false},{"id":"e01p2414","s":"Susan","t":"What does this mean?","r":true,"m":["What does this mean? 这是什么意思？更侧重于单纯地询问意思，较为客观。","What’s that supposed to mean?更多包含说话者的主观情绪，对含义有所质疑。"]},{"id":"e01p2415","s":"Lynette","t":"I don't know. But check out the postmark.","r":true,"m":["postmark n. 邮戳"]},{"id":"e01p2416","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, my god. She got it the day she died.","r":true},{"id":"e01p2417","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Do you think this is why she ... ?","r":false},{"id":"e01p2418","s":"Alice","t":"I'm so sorry, girls. I never wanted you to be burdened with this.","r":true,"m":["burden n. 负担，责任；负重，负荷；be burdened with 背负着；承担着"]},{"id":"e01p2419","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, Mary Alice, what did you do?","r":true}]}]};
